<title>JAPAN: Sega says plans to sell TV-telephone system.</title>
<headline>Sega says plans to sell TV-telephone system.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sega Enterprises Ltd said on Friday that it would start selling a home-use TV-telephone system compatible with Sega's Saturn videogame players.</p>
<p>A Sega official in charge of multimedia services said the system would allow transmission of graphics and voice data.</p>
<p>He said the system could go on sale as early as next year, but did not provide any other details.</p>
</text>
